# HARD RULE — Verification Pipeline (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

Every task, without exception, MUST complete this exact sequence before being
marked done. Skipping ANY step means the task is NOT verified and stays open.

## The Pipeline (in order)

### 1. ISOLATED TEST (required first)
- Build a dedicated `scenes/<feature>_test/<feature>_test.tscn` + `.gd`
- Self-contained: no main scene, no arena, no HUD dependencies
- Write `user://selftest_report.json` with verdict + screenshot paths
- Call `get_tree().quit()` when done
- Run: `run_selftest.ps1 -RequestPath ... -Scene res://scenes/<x>/<x>.tscn`
- **Read EVERY screenshot** with the Read tool — not just the report

### 2. IN-GAME TEST (required second)
- Run in the actual game via the main scene
- Use dev commands / selftest requests to trigger the feature
- **Read EVERY screenshot** with the Read tool

### 3. BEFORE/AFTER SCREENSHOT PAIR (required for visual changes)
- BEFORE: revert the change (or use pre-change screenshot if available)
- AFTER: with the change applied
- Both must be captured in the SAME mode (isolated AND in-game if possible)
- If the change was already made, temporarily revert → capture → re-apply → capture
- Commit both to `tools/selftest/results/`

### 4. PLAN.md STATUS UPDATE (required last)
- Update the task's status line in PLAN.md
- Mark checkboxes for completed sub-items
- Reference the screenshot paths in the status

### 5. COMMIT + PUSH (required)
- `git add -A` (include ALL screenshots + report JSONs)
- `git commit -m "task description"`
- `git push`

## Checklist Template (copy-paste into your todo)

For each task, create these sub-items and complete ALL of them:
- [ ] Isolated test scene built and passing
- [ ] Isolated screenshots read (Read tool on each .png)
- [ ] In-game test run
- [ ] In-game screenshots read (Read tool on each .png)
- [ ] Before/after pair captured (isolated + in-game if visual)
- [ ] PLAN.md status updated
- [ ] All screenshots committed to git
- [ ] Pushed to remote

## NO EXCEPTIONS

- "It's a simple change" → still run the full pipeline
- "The isolated test already exists" → still run it fresh + read screenshots
- "The in-game test is hard" → build the observation first (dev command, probe)
- "I'm confident it works" → confidence is NOT verification, screenshots are
- **"I already have an in-game test" → IRRELEVANT. The isolated test MUST come first. An
  existing in-game test does NOT satisfy step 1. Build the isolated scene (or an isolated
  probe) and run it BEFORE any in-game run, even if the in-game test is faster.**
- **Order is enforced: you may only move to IN-GAME (step 2) after the ISOLATED test
  (step 1) has passed and its screenshots have been read. If you find yourself about to
  run an in-game test and have not done the isolated test in THIS task's session, STOP
  and do the isolated test first.**

## When a step fails

- Fix the root cause, re-run that step
- Do NOT skip the failed step
- Do NOT mark the task done while any step is red
